{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01J7bW8D8NfhkEuWivth9xpK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed as `b5328a8`. Ralph infra files (`.ralph/`, `.ralphrc`) untouched.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis loop I completed the next pending autonomous task: **wiring `stereo-split.ts` into the mixer as a \"Split L/R\" control**.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Confirmed `stereo-split.ts` (M/S sub-split DSP) was fully implemented and unit-tested but had zero UI reachability — dead code.\n2. Added an off-render `useEffect` in `StemsView` that runs `analyzePanContent` across loaded stems and tracks the ids with meaningful side energy (`hasPannedContent`) — gating avoids per-render O(samples) cost.\n3. Added `handleSplitStereo`: M/S-decodes a stem via `stereoSplit`, builds two mono AudioBuffers, and replaces the parent with two hard-panned (−1 / +1) L/R sub-stems in both the store and the engine.\n4. Rendered a gated \"Split L/R\" per-stem button block (distinct from the backend-based \"Split Further\").\n5. Extracted the track-construction logic into the pure `buildStereoSubTracks` helper (`src/lib/mix/split-stereo-tracks.ts`) so the naming/pan/preserved-field decisions are testable without an AudioContext — 6 unit tests.\n\n**Green gate:** `tsc` clean, `eslint .` clean, 16/16 affected tests passing.\n\n**Genuinely remaining autonomous tasks:** Pro Mode denser spectrum (`SpectrumDisplay` `pro` density prop), and `MasterScreen` component extraction.\n\n```\n---RALPH_STATUS---\nSTATUS: IN_PROGRESS\nTASKS_COMPLETED_THIS_LOOP: 1\nFILES_MODIFIED: 4\nTESTS_STATUS: PASSING\nWORK_TYPE: IMPLEMENTATION\nEXIT_SIGNAL: false\nRECOMMENDATION: Next loop, add a `pro` density prop to SpectrumDisplay driven by proMode so Pro Mode shows a denser spectrum (the next pending autonomous item).\n---END_RALPH_STATUS---\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":683,"cac